  "description": "UKANAW crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group F d d d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C74 H80 Dy4 N8 O30,4(C2 H3 N1),12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1M (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1G (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1J (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.589-3.832 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.75-109.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(HL)4(C6H4NH2COO)2(μ3-OH)4(μ-OH)2(H2O)4]·4CH3CN·12H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
